METHOD. Three independent neuters. Each one breaks a DIFFERENT load-bearing
part of the engine, and for each the observation is a RED that NAMES the arm
that caught it. Restores are a byte-for-byte 'cp' from the backup above,
verified by sha256 equality AND by grepping the newest Task-2 export
(FIXTURE_ALLOWLIST) back out of the restored file. No blanket working-tree
restore is used anywhere in this harness — such a command discards
uncommitted work silently, which is exactly what a neuter/restore harness
must never do.

